      <ReturnValue>
        <ReturnType>Microsoft.Build.Framework.ITaskItem</ReturnType>
      </ReturnValue>
      <Docs>
        <summary>
            Gets or sets a <see cref="T:Microsoft.Build.Framework.ITaskItem" /> with a destination folder path to untar the files to.
            </summary>
        <value>To be added.</value>
        <remarks>
            The path parameters are exposed as <see cref="T:Microsoft.Build.Framework.ITaskItem" /> rather than <see cref="T:System.IO.DirectoryInfo" />/
            <see cref="T:System.IO.FileInfo" /> so that .NET Framework MSBuild can reflect over this task's parameters when
            dispatching it to the .NET task host. That inspection resolves parameter types through a
            <c>MetadataLoadContext</c> in which the only available core assembly is .NET Framework's, whose
            <c>System.Runtime</c> facade does not forward <see cref="T:System.IO.FileInfo" /> or <see cref="T:System.IO.DirectoryInfo" />.
            </remarks>
      </Docs>
    </Member>
